sbook><name>TAKIYAMA SHIGEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASAHARA, HIDEMITSU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MARUO CALCIUM COMPANY LIMITED</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MINAYOSHI, SHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKIYAMA, SHIGEO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KASAHARA HIDEMITSU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MINAYOSHI SHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKIYAMA SHIGEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASAHARA, HIDEMITSU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MINAYOSHI, SHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKIYAMA, SHIGEO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An additive for synthetic resins characterized by comprising a composite comprising particles (M) having a porous petaloid structure as a support and a calcium phosphate compound (R) deposited on the support, and by having a specific form and a specific heating loss. The additive has excellent transparency, scratch resistance, and anti-blocking properties and can give a synthetic resin composition extremely reduced in discoloration caused by resin deterioration and a synthetic resin having excellent dyeability.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un additif pour résine synthétique caractérisé en ce qu'il contient un composite à base de particules (M) présentant une structure pétaloïde poreuse utilisée comme support et un composé de phosphate de calcium (R) déposé sur le support, et en ce qu'il présente une forme spécifique et une perte à la chaleur spécifique. Cet additif présente d'excellentes propriétés en terme de transparence, de résistance à la rayure, et d'antiblocage, et permet d'obtenir une résine synthétique d'excellente réceptivité à la peinture, à coloration extrêmement réduite due à la détérioration de la résine.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>